WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:16.165
want to ask Jev to help us spy on Morb?"

2
00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:19.327
Zann stared at Gliss, hardly believing his ears.

3
00:00:19.347 --> 00:00:21.129
"Are you kidding?"

4
00:00:21.149 --> 00:00:23.871
"Maybe Gliss is right," Perda said.

5
00:00:23.891 --> 00:00:26.553
"I know Jev's not your favorite person, Zann.

6
00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.774
But he's good at magic."

7
00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:30.335
"So what?"

8
00:00:30.715 --> 00:00:31.216
Zann said.

9
00:00:31.568 --> 00:00:33.189
"Lots of people are good at magic.

10
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.251
We could ask your parents to help instead.

11
00:00:37.051 --> 00:00:39.213
Or maybe one of our teachers or the mayor."

12
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:44.476
"It would take too long to explain everything to them," Gliss pointed out.

13
00:00:44.496 --> 00:00:48.638
"Besides, Jev will definitely do it if I ask him."

14
00:00:49.378 --> 00:00:53.381
Zann couldn't believe the girls were seriously thinking about going to Jev for help.

15
00:00:54.061 --> 00:00:57.243
He glanced at Darb, expecting his friend to be on his side.

16
00:00:57.903 --> 00:00:59.024
Darb had a thoughtful look.

17
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.502
"Well, it's not a bad idea," he said.

18
00:01:02.522 --> 00:01:05.364
"Let's go find him," Perda said.

19
00:01:05.905 --> 00:01:09.667
Before Zann could say another word, the others were hurrying out of the Hollow.

20
00:01:11.849 --> 00:01:13.330
He had little choice but to follow.

21
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:17.273
Soon they were all hiding in a clump of trees near Jev's house.

22
00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:22.176
Jev was in the yard playing with his pet dragon, but they didn't dare call to him.

23
00:01:22.837 --> 00:01:27.380
By now it was afternoon, and there were a lot more people around than there had been earlier.

24
00:01:28.428 --> 00:01:31.650
They all knew that Morb could be awake and lurking out there somewhere.

25
00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:36.032
"I wish we could just use a Summoning spell," Perda complained.

26
00:01:36.753 --> 00:01:38.674
"Living without magic is hard!"

27
00:01:38.694 --> 00:01:40.155
"I have an idea."

28
00:01:40.815 --> 00:01:43.316
Darb reached into his pocket for a pencil and paper.

29
00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:47.058
Scribbling a note, he held it out to Zing.

30
00:01:47.699 --> 00:01:49.540
"Take this to Jev, okay, buddy?"

31
00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.222
At first Zing didn't understand what Darb wanted.

32
00:01:53.882 --> 00:01:56.644
He tried to eat the note, and then he tried to roast it.

33
00:01:57.388 --> 00:01:58.849
But finally he figured it out.

34
00:02:01.351 --> 00:02:03.072
Jev looked up when the dragon flew at him.

35
00:02:03.092 --> 00:02:05.294
"Shoo! You'll scare Hazi."

36
00:02:05.994 --> 00:02:06.654
Then he blinked.

37
00:02:06.674 --> 00:02:07.595
"Wait a minute.

38
00:02:07.995 --> 00:02:11.798
Aren't you Zing whistled and dropped the note by Jev's feet.

39
00:02:12.518 --> 00:02:13.959
Jev grabbed the paper and read it.

40
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.682
A second later he picked up his dragon and headed toward his house.

41
00:02:17.702 --> 00:02:20.144
"See?" Zann whispered.

42
00:02:20.164 --> 00:02:21.825
"He's ignoring the note!

43
00:02:22.665 --> 00:02:26.108
I told you he was—" "Wait," Gliss interrupted.

44
00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.733
"He's just putting his dragon inside."

45
00:02:29.494 --> 00:02:31.975
Sure enough, Jev was already hurrying toward them.

46
00:02:32.635 --> 00:02:35.077
When he heard what they wanted, he smirked at Zann.

47
00:02:35.097 --> 00:02:40.019
"Wow, it must be tough living with no magic like a Void all day, huh?"

48
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:40.700
he said.

49
00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.342
"Especially for a snooty Red like you."

50
00:02:44.362 --> 00:02:46.623
"Will you help us, Jev?"

51
00:02:47.103 --> 00:02:48.604
Gliss asked, grabbing his arm.

52
00:02:48.624 --> 00:02:52.386
"Please?" Jev glanced down at her hand on his arm.

53
00:02:52.406 --> 00:02:55.368
"Um, sure," he said.

54
00:02:55.884 --> 00:02:56.965
"I was just kidding around.

55
00:02:57.966 --> 00:02:58.826
What do you want me to do?"

56
00:02:59.547 --> 00:03:02.989
It didn't take long for Jev to summon and send a spy fly to Morb.

57
00:03:03.689 --> 00:03:09.874
Zann watched the whole process, chafing silently at seeing his enemy do magic when he himself was powerless.

58
00:03:09.894 --> 00:03:12.615
"Thanks, Jev," Perda said.

59
00:03:12.635 --> 00:03:15.878
"Can you come find us in the Hollow when the spy fly returns?"

60
00:03:15.898 --> 00:03:17.199
"The Hollow?"

61
00:03:17.479 --> 00:03:18.780
Jev looked a little nervous.

62
00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:20.361
"Sure, I guess."

63
00:03:21.161 --> 00:03:23.823
Just then he noticed Gliss rubbing her stomach.

64
00:03:23.843 --> 00:03:25.104
"Are you hungry?

65
00:03:25.512 --> 00:03:26.833
I could conjure up some lunch."

66
00:03:26.853 --> 00:03:28.915
"That would be great!"

67
00:03:29.316 --> 00:03:29.796
Gliss said.

68
00:03:29.816 --> 00:03:32.318
"We haven't eaten since yesterday."

69
00:03:33.619 --> 00:03:37.943
She talked him into conjuring up enough food for all of them, along with some fresh clothes.

70
00:03:39.124 --> 00:03:41.526
After that they left Jev and headed for the Hollow.

71
00:03:42.227 --> 00:03:44.008
When they got there, Zing whimpered.

72
00:03:44.028 --> 00:03:47.271
"I know, Zing," said Zann with a sigh.

73
00:03:47.291 --> 00:03:49.473
"I don't like being here either.

74
00:03:50.294 --> 00:03:52.296
But it's safer than being out in the open."

75
00:03:53.364 --> 00:03:56.465
"How long do you think it will take the spy fly to get there and back?"

76
00:03:56.805 --> 00:03:57.385
Gliss asked.

77
00:03:58.085 --> 00:03:58.926
The others shrugged.

78
00:03:59.666 --> 00:04:01.226
Spy flies were very fast.

79
00:04:01.566 --> 00:04:05.728
Like message moths they could zap themselves long distances when necessary.

80
00:04:06.508 --> 00:04:10.269
But there was no way of telling how long it would take the little creature to find Morb

81
00:04:10.569 --> 00:04:11.789
and observe what he was doing.

82
00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:15.650
By now Morb had probably woken up and left Zann's house.

83
00:04:16.691 --> 00:04:18.191
Zann pulled out Boz's diary.

84
00:04:18.211 --> 00:04:21.052
"Guess I'll start reading this while we're waiting.

85
00:04:22.092 --> 00:04:25.534
Maybe we can figure out whether it's still worth trying to get it to the palace."

86
00:04:26.394 --> 00:04:30.476
"Too bad none of us can do an advanced Restore spell yet," Perda said.

87
00:04:30.496 --> 00:04:33.917
"Maybe we could take the diary to Professor Liblow."

88
00:04:33.937 --> 00:04:38.339
"It was dangerous enough to leave the Hollow to find Jev," Darb said.

89
00:04:38.359 --> 00:04:41.260
"Morb and his trolls could be anywhere."

90
00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.841
"He's right," Zann agreed.

91
00:04:43.861 --> 00:04:48.043
"Besides, we don't even know if we need a Restore spell yet."

92
00:04:48.823 --> 00:04:50.964
Zann opened the diary to the first page.

93
00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:55.886
For a moment he just stared at his grandfather's familiar, loopy handwriting.

94
00:04:56.667 --> 00:05:03.050
Zann had always found it strange that Boz, a highly accomplished Magic Master, chose to record his life

95
00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.772
in such an old-fashioned and non-magical way.

96
00:05:06.852 --> 00:05:09.434
Pushing that thought aside, Zann started to read.

97
00:05:10.134 --> 00:05:12.295
The diary began before Zann was born.

98
00:05:13.056 --> 00:05:19.799
In fact, one of the earliest entries mentioned Zann's mother— Boz's daughter—meeting a handsome young explorer.

99
00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:23.549
"Dad," Zann murmured, tracing his father's name.

100
00:05:24.309 --> 00:05:27.450
It was tempting to read everything about his parents' early days together.

101
00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:29.731
He knew he didn't have time though.

102
00:05:30.691 --> 00:05:34.752
He skimmed over some entries about Boz's day-to-day life as a Magic Master.

103
00:05:35.432 --> 00:05:42.514
They were surprisingly boring, but then Zann saw pages filled with stories about his parents' explorations and adventures.

104
00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:47.456
"I can go back and read those later, when Boz is safe," he told himself.

105
00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:53.765
He tore his gaze away from a description of his own third birthday party and continued flipping through

106
00:05:53.785 --> 00:05:54.305
the diary.

107
00:05:55.046 --> 00:05:56.607
The next few pages were missing.

108
00:05:57.287 --> 00:06:03.593
When Zann turned to the next legible page, a familiar name jumped out at him; in bold, angry

109
00:06:03.653 --> 00:06:05.915
letters, his grandfather had scrawled
